WEBVTT

00:00:01.080 --> 00:00:04.830
On my journey with Akari,
we stopped by the port city of Libelle.

00:00:05.130 --> 00:00:10.170
Off the coast of the city was a prison of fog with one
of the Four Major Human Errors sealed within:

00:00:10.170 --> 00:00:12.000
The Pandemonium.

00:00:12.420 --> 00:00:17.630
I attempted to trap Akari within the
Pandemonium to dispose of her,

00:00:17.630 --> 00:00:23.290
<i>but Akari used her Pure Concept of [Time]
</i>to return as if nothing had happened.<b></b>

00:02:05.500 --> 00:02:09.790
<b>Episode 8: Monstrine</b>

00:02:10.210 --> 00:02:11.630
It's so pretty!

00:02:11.630 --> 00:02:14.580
Akari, don't stick yourself out like that.

00:02:15.250 --> 00:02:19.330
It reminds me of when I almost
drowned a long time ago.

00:02:20.380 --> 00:02:23.080
You fell in the ocean before, Menou?!

00:02:23.330 --> 00:02:26.460
It was back when I was little, here in this city.

00:02:26.460 --> 00:02:28.830
In Libelle? You never told me that!

00:02:28.830 --> 00:02:32.420
I'm sure you were cute even if you were drowning!

00:02:32.420 --> 00:02:33.540
Are you kidding?

00:02:33.790 --> 00:02:34.790
Any other memories?

00:02:41.460 --> 00:02:46.250
This was where I found out that Master Flare
was an Executioner who killed otherworlders.

00:02:46.920 --> 00:02:49.960
Nothing in particular. It was a long time ago.

00:02:52.750 --> 00:02:54.460
<b>Café</b>

00:02:54.540 --> 00:02:57.380
There you are, Flarette.

00:03:01.880 --> 00:03:03.420
Wow!

00:03:03.630 --> 00:03:05.500
It's so lively!

00:03:05.500 --> 00:03:09.040
It's not just tourists. The locals frequent this place, too.

00:03:09.250 --> 00:03:12.210
It's probably the most crowded place in town.

00:03:13.040 --> 00:03:15.250
Fish... Fruit...

00:03:17.670 --> 00:03:19.210
What are those things?

00:03:19.210 --> 00:03:20.330
They're etheric tools.

00:03:20.330 --> 00:03:21.630
"Etheric tools"?

00:03:21.920 --> 00:03:24.420
They're items that channel magecraft.

00:03:24.420 --> 00:03:27.880
I think those were probably
unearthed from an ancient ruin.

00:03:28.250 --> 00:03:32.170
Towns that are adjacent to the Wild Frontier
have these kinds of shops that-

00:03:32.420 --> 00:03:34.000
Hey, Akari?!

00:03:34.500 --> 00:03:35.790
Thank you!

00:03:38.330 --> 00:03:40.710
Jeez, you're the one who asked the question.

00:03:40.710 --> 00:03:43.790
Here, Menou. Open up!

00:03:44.170 --> 00:03:46.750
Take that!

00:03:52.250 --> 00:03:54.040
What?! It's so good!

00:03:54.040 --> 00:03:55.170
It's watermelon.

00:03:55.960 --> 00:03:57.540
Wait, watermelon?

00:03:57.540 --> 00:04:01.250
It's a little different from the watermelon I know,

00:04:01.250 --> 00:04:04.380
but yeah, I guess the flavor is close to watermelon...

00:04:04.670 --> 00:04:07.670
What's different about the watermelon you know?

00:04:07.670 --> 00:04:09.250
Let's see, it's usually red, though sometimes yellow...

00:04:09.250 --> 00:04:12.670
That man... He looks like he's just walking,
Let's see, it's usually red, though sometimes yellow...<b></b>

00:04:12.670 --> 00:04:13.290
That man... He looks like he's just walking,
And there are seeds all over,<b></b>

00:04:13.290 --> 00:04:14.250
but it's obvious he's monitoring us.
And there are seeds all over,<b></b>

00:04:14.250 --> 00:04:15.750
but it's obvious he's monitoring us.
just enough so they don't get in the way of eating...<b></b>

00:04:15.750 --> 00:04:17.080
just enough so they don't get in the way of eating...

00:04:21.500 --> 00:04:22.330
<b><i>Invoke</i></b>

00:04:22.330 --> 00:04:23.420
<b><i>[Flameshot]</i></b>

00:04:28.710 --> 00:04:30.380
<b><i>Barrier</i></b>

00:04:29.000 --> 00:04:30.580
What is this, Menou?!

00:04:30.580 --> 00:04:32.420
Please calm down, everyone.

00:04:32.420 --> 00:04:33.670
Get down on the ground!

00:04:33.790 --> 00:04:35.420
Why here, of all places?

00:04:35.750 --> 00:04:37.670
Akari, will you hold this for me?

00:04:38.380 --> 00:04:41.040
M-Menou! What do I do with this?!

00:04:46.130 --> 00:04:47.130
Stop right there.

00:04:51.420 --> 00:04:54.500
I would say you live up to your
name as Flare's apprentice,

00:04:54.500 --> 00:04:56.000
but you forgot something important.

00:04:56.000 --> 00:04:58.670
S-sorry, Menou...

00:04:58.670 --> 00:05:01.000
You're part of the Fourth, aren't you?

00:05:01.000 --> 00:05:04.420
This is an awfully aggressive welcome,
but what do you want?

00:05:04.420 --> 00:05:08.250
We want to eliminate you of course, Flarette.

00:05:08.670 --> 00:05:11.580
I see. So they're not after Akari.

00:05:11.960 --> 00:05:14.380
How do you know who I am?

00:05:14.380 --> 00:05:19.580
We got word that you thwarted some of our
comrades who were active in Grisarika.

00:05:19.580 --> 00:05:22.630
We've had our eyes on you ever since.

00:05:22.960 --> 00:05:28.170
You mean those terrorists on the train?
They were members of the Fourth, too?

00:05:28.170 --> 00:05:32.040
Now that you mention it, I see the resemblance.
Like your amateurish tactics.

00:05:32.330 --> 00:05:33.580
Why, you...

00:05:33.580 --> 00:05:36.130
Don't you understand the situation you're in?!

00:05:37.040 --> 00:05:40.000
Actually, you're the one who doesn't seem to understand.

00:05:40.630 --> 00:05:42.330
That idiot is just a decoy.

00:05:54.790 --> 00:05:55.710
Die, you!

00:05:58.540 --> 00:05:59.630
You little...!

00:06:01.460 --> 00:06:02.210
There.

00:06:02.460 --> 00:06:03.790
That takes care of them.

00:06:03.790 --> 00:06:05.380
Amazing as always, Menou!

00:06:05.380 --> 00:06:06.290
Here!

00:06:06.290 --> 00:06:09.170
Hey! Where are the ruffians?!

00:06:09.170 --> 00:06:11.460
The knights are finally here.

00:06:12.460 --> 00:06:14.750
Well, that was a surprise.

00:06:14.750 --> 00:06:19.460
He did say he would attack her,
but I never thought it would be right after the meeting.

00:06:20.130 --> 00:06:21.790
So that's Flarette.

00:06:21.790 --> 00:06:24.630
I believe the other girl called her "Menou"?

00:06:25.420 --> 00:06:28.710
<i>Beautiful and strong... It hardly seems fair.</i>

00:06:28.880 --> 00:06:31.250
Oh, can I take this, please?

00:06:31.710 --> 00:06:36.170
Those two are definitely going to talk, aren't they?

00:06:36.170 --> 00:06:37.420
Besides...

00:06:37.790 --> 00:06:41.710
He's the one who spoke ill
of my mother during the meeting.

00:06:47.290 --> 00:06:48.880
Hey, what's wrong?!

00:06:55.790 --> 00:06:58.040
What should we do now, Menou?!

00:06:58.040 --> 00:07:01.710
Well, the church needs me there this evening, but-

00:07:02.630 --> 00:07:03.790
What was that?

00:07:03.790 --> 00:07:05.170
You stay here, Akari!

00:07:07.750 --> 00:07:09.170
What happened?!

00:07:09.670 --> 00:07:11.960
Th-they suddenly transformed into monsters...

00:07:11.960 --> 00:07:13.330
"Monsters"?

00:07:22.580 --> 00:07:24.250
That's delicious!

00:07:29.500 --> 00:07:30.540
You may enter.

00:07:31.170 --> 00:07:32.580
Excuse me.

00:07:34.630 --> 00:07:36.330
You must be Ms. Menou.

00:07:36.330 --> 00:07:38.380
Yes, Pastor Sicilia.

00:07:38.380 --> 00:07:40.420
It's an honor to meet you.

00:07:40.960 --> 00:07:42.830
No need for compliments.

00:07:43.710 --> 00:07:47.880
I heard you made a big show of
fighting in the market earlier.

00:07:47.880 --> 00:07:48.830
I did.

00:07:49.170 --> 00:07:50.670
I can't say I'm impressed,

00:07:50.670 --> 00:07:54.420
given you're an Executioner
with an otherworlder with you.

00:07:54.420 --> 00:07:56.500
The situation was unavoidable.

00:07:56.500 --> 00:07:59.880
And afterwards, I came across a number of odd things.

00:08:00.210 --> 00:08:05.790
Is that so. But first, let's discuss this odd item here.

00:08:04.630 --> 00:08:06.040
<b>Expense Approval Form</b>

00:08:07.580 --> 00:08:10.420
Your approval form for travel funds...

00:08:10.710 --> 00:08:14.290
It doesn't specify the most important detail:

00:08:14.290 --> 00:08:17.210
how you intend to dispose of
your otherworlder companion.

00:08:17.420 --> 00:08:18.580
Well...

00:08:19.000 --> 00:08:22.920
You don't actually intend on taking
her to the Sanctuary, do you?

00:08:22.920 --> 00:08:26.250
There's no such place that
"takes otherworlders in," after all.

00:08:26.500 --> 00:08:29.710
I'm continuing to look for a way to kill her!

00:08:29.710 --> 00:08:32.460
I promise I'll find a way before we get to the Sanctuary!

00:08:32.540 --> 00:08:37.290
So you want more money for this journey
based on such an ambiguous promise?

00:08:37.710 --> 00:08:40.250
You have got to be kidding me.

00:08:41.170 --> 00:08:46.630
However, if it's a fair transaction where
I compensate you for your labor,

00:08:46.630 --> 00:08:48.960
there might be a way.

00:08:49.580 --> 00:08:53.040
I see, so the usual, then.

00:08:53.750 --> 00:08:56.210
What do I need to investigate?

00:08:56.960 --> 00:08:58.750
"Monstrine"?

00:08:56.960 --> 00:08:59.380
<b>Libelle</b>

00:08:58.750 --> 00:09:01.830
Yes, because it's "monstrous," I suppose.

00:09:01.830 --> 00:09:06.080
It's a drug that's being dealt around
town that supposedly induces euphoria.

00:09:06.380 --> 00:09:08.130
Here's a sample.

00:09:08.130 --> 00:09:10.460
Wait, this etheric reaction...

00:09:10.630 --> 00:09:12.880
It's sin magecraft!

00:09:12.880 --> 00:09:14.080
Exactly.

00:09:14.210 --> 00:09:21.380
And invoking sin magecraft most often
involves a human body, spirit, or soul.

00:09:21.670 --> 00:09:22.540
Which means...

00:09:22.540 --> 00:09:25.710
...there are people being sacrificed.

00:09:26.170 --> 00:09:28.000
How despicable.

00:09:28.000 --> 00:09:29.040
Yes...

00:09:29.040 --> 00:09:34.580
But the odd thing is that there are very few
people who have gone missing in this city.

00:09:34.880 --> 00:09:37.960
Maybe they were just never reported missing?

00:09:37.960 --> 00:09:40.080
That's not all that's odd.

00:09:40.380 --> 00:09:43.540
I actually got attacked by the Fourth earlier.

00:09:43.540 --> 00:09:45.580
What?! Really?

00:09:45.710 --> 00:09:49.380
After they got captured they turned into monsters.

00:09:49.380 --> 00:09:53.500
According to Pastor Sicilia,
it has something to do with this "monstrine."

00:09:53.750 --> 00:09:55.460
Why would they turn some of their own?

00:09:55.460 --> 00:10:00.460
In any case, we have to investigate.
For the sake of travel funds, as well.

00:10:01.080 --> 00:10:03.960
Could you look into the supply chain, Momo?

00:10:03.960 --> 00:10:04.960
Sure.

00:10:05.080 --> 00:10:09.880
I'm happy to do anything that makes
things easier for you, Menou.

00:10:09.880 --> 00:10:13.380
Though it really ticks me off that it's for
your journey with that stupid set of boobs!

00:10:13.380 --> 00:10:15.130
Thank you, Momo.

00:10:15.670 --> 00:10:17.580
More! I want more pats on the head!

00:10:17.580 --> 00:10:19.880
While you're looking into that,
More! I want more pats on the head!<b></b>

00:10:19.880 --> 00:10:22.000
I'll investigate from a different angle.

00:10:22.080 --> 00:10:23.500
<b>Libelle</b>

00:10:30.880 --> 00:10:33.330
What?! I can't see anything in front of me!

00:10:33.330 --> 00:10:34.580
Oh, come on...

00:10:34.960 --> 00:10:36.040
Whoops?

00:10:36.170 --> 00:10:39.080
Splash! Shake shake shake.

00:10:39.460 --> 00:10:41.250
Good morning, Menou!

00:10:41.960 --> 00:10:44.710
You got away!

00:10:46.880 --> 00:10:47.750
Akari...

00:10:48.250 --> 00:10:50.830
Were you planning to crush me
to death with your weight?

00:10:50.830 --> 00:10:51.960
Excuse me?!

00:10:52.130 --> 00:10:55.920
You were taking so long to get up,
so I just figured I'd wake you up!

00:10:56.880 --> 00:10:59.960
I'm sure there were better ways to wake me up.

00:11:00.710 --> 00:11:03.790
I got carried away with my love for you!

00:11:03.790 --> 00:11:06.920
Hey, owww!

00:11:09.170 --> 00:11:12.710
But it's so unusual, you know? You waking up so late!

00:11:12.710 --> 00:11:14.830
Well, I suppose so.

00:11:14.830 --> 00:11:18.130
Is it because the pastor wanted you at the church?

00:11:18.540 --> 00:11:20.710
Did you two get up to some "fun" last night?

00:11:20.710 --> 00:11:21.710
Ow!

00:11:21.710 --> 00:11:22.630
Oof...

00:11:22.960 --> 00:11:26.330
The figurehead of the Fourth in this city, Manon Libelle...

00:11:26.710 --> 00:11:30.460
I need to find a way to investigate her affairs...

00:11:31.000 --> 00:11:32.130
But how?

00:11:32.380 --> 00:11:36.420
Lady Manon, you're the one who suggested
we distribute that monstrine!

00:11:36.540 --> 00:11:38.710
Yes, that's quite correct.

00:11:39.420 --> 00:11:43.380
Monstrine provides euphoria and is
highly addictive to those who take it.

00:11:43.460 --> 00:11:47.290
That's what you said when you brought
in that etheric tool for producing it!

00:11:47.290 --> 00:11:52.830
Yes, the drug for distribution has
been adjusted to be that way.

00:11:52.830 --> 00:11:56.000
Not only is it a way to fund our activities,

00:11:56.000 --> 00:12:01.170
but those who take it can potentially be
used as hostages to stave off the Faust.

00:12:01.630 --> 00:12:03.380
As a final resort,

00:12:03.380 --> 00:12:05.830
we could turn them into monsters
and use them as weapons.

00:12:06.000 --> 00:12:07.790
That's what you said.

00:12:07.790 --> 00:12:09.290
I did.

00:12:09.670 --> 00:12:13.170
In that case, why did Kaiser turn into a monster?!

00:12:13.500 --> 00:12:15.330
He's a member of our council!

00:12:15.330 --> 00:12:16.670
Kaiser...?

00:12:18.460 --> 00:12:23.460
Oh, you mean the man from yesterday!
The reason is simple enough.

00:12:23.460 --> 00:12:26.960
I laced the food I served during
the meetings with monstrine.

00:12:27.080 --> 00:12:27.920
What?!

00:12:28.000 --> 00:12:29.420
What have you done?!

00:12:29.960 --> 00:12:31.130
Why you little...!

00:12:31.380 --> 00:12:33.040
You won't get away with this!

00:12:39.540 --> 00:12:44.210
<b><i>Ether: Living Sacrifice - Chaos Adhesion</i></b>

00:12:39.540 --> 00:12:44.210
<b><i>Pure Concept [Chaos] - Summon</i></b>

00:12:39.540 --> 00:12:44.210
<b><i>[Tangled Jump Rope]</i></b>

00:13:11.250 --> 00:13:14.920
So, um, are there any other complaints?

00:13:15.380 --> 00:13:19.500
You're a failure who never inherited your mother's power.
How dare you?

00:13:23.250 --> 00:13:25.130
It's simple, really.

00:13:25.880 --> 00:13:29.210
A certain individual asked me to spread monstrine,

00:13:29.210 --> 00:13:33.710
in return for help in enacting my revenge.

00:13:33.710 --> 00:13:35.170
"Revenge"?

00:13:35.170 --> 00:13:39.670
Flarette, the apprentice to Flare, who killed my mother.

00:13:40.210 --> 00:13:42.330
Once I knew she was coming,

00:13:42.330 --> 00:13:47.420
it was only natural that I wanted to give her a
"proper" welcome, don't you think?

00:13:50.670 --> 00:13:56.210
I'm making all kinds of arrangements,
so I do hope you'll all cooperate.

00:14:16.380 --> 00:14:20.210
Hey, cut that out! What did we ever do to you?!

00:14:20.210 --> 00:14:23.630
Like I said, just tell me what you know.

00:14:24.960 --> 00:14:30.000
You lot are the dregs of society.
You must have used monstrine, no?

00:14:30.000 --> 00:14:33.130
W-we've got nothin' to do with that!

00:14:33.130 --> 00:14:36.380
Our leader told us never to touch the stuff!

00:14:37.960 --> 00:14:42.750
A delinquent leader with morals?
I'd love to see the person's face!

00:14:42.750 --> 00:14:44.000
This way, Leader!

00:14:44.080 --> 00:14:45.880
I know, calm down.

00:14:46.960 --> 00:14:48.000
Wait, this voice...

00:14:48.330 --> 00:14:52.920
Hey, whoever you are,
I won't have you messing with my...

00:14:54.380 --> 00:14:58.130
Well, if it isn't Momo!
To think we'd reunite in a place like this!

00:15:00.040 --> 00:15:04.000
You die here, crappy little princess!

00:15:05.130 --> 00:15:09.080
I must say, I'm so glad we get to talk like this, Momo.

00:15:10.040 --> 00:15:12.540
Once my initial surprise attack failed,

00:15:12.540 --> 00:15:16.170
I knew prolonging the fight would
only please you, Little Princess.

00:15:16.170 --> 00:15:20.080
You've come to know me too well, Momo.

00:15:22.290 --> 00:15:25.290
Why couldn't you have died in those ruins?!

00:15:25.290 --> 00:15:29.420
Oh, those gargoyles there were quite a challenge.

00:15:29.750 --> 00:15:32.790
Enemies based on the concept
of original sin are troublesome.

00:15:32.790 --> 00:15:35.630
I'm especially poorly matched against demons.

00:15:35.630 --> 00:15:38.290
Because your only strategy is brute force.

00:15:38.580 --> 00:15:42.670
Though gargoyles are inferior,
just stone statues with demons infused in them.

00:15:42.670 --> 00:15:45.420
They're actually closer to monsters than demons.

00:15:45.880 --> 00:15:47.580
Oh, is that so?

00:15:47.580 --> 00:15:51.670
They're inanimate objects that had their
composition changed by taking in demons.

00:15:51.670 --> 00:15:56.710
Monsters are basically creatures that have
mutated by taking in original sin, after all.

00:15:56.710 --> 00:16:00.250
I never gave thought to what monsters might be.

00:16:00.250 --> 00:16:02.790
Of course you didn't, Little Princess.

00:16:03.540 --> 00:16:08.130
Well, until about a thousand years
ago before sin magecraft existed,

00:16:08.130 --> 00:16:11.580
demons and monsters didn't even exist, you know?

00:16:11.960 --> 00:16:13.960
What happened a thousand years ago?

00:16:13.960 --> 00:16:16.790
There's no reason I should have to explain this, but fine.

00:16:18.380 --> 00:16:22.580
You know the Pandemonium that's
off the coast of this city?

00:16:22.580 --> 00:16:26.540
Yes, it's the fog that has one of the
Four Major Human Errors sealed within.

00:16:26.830 --> 00:16:31.880
That Human Error was originally a
very young girl from another world.

00:16:32.380 --> 00:16:37.080
With her Pure Concept,
the girl's fantasies materialized into demons,

00:16:37.080 --> 00:16:40.580
and the blood and flesh that
fell from her became monsters.

00:16:41.250 --> 00:16:47.130
<i>An inferior imitation of her Pure Concept [Chaos]
</i>became what we know as sin magecraft.<b></b>

00:16:47.880 --> 00:16:48.960
In other words,

00:16:48.960 --> 00:16:55.380
the thing sealed within the Pandemonium is the
very source of the monsters that ravage our world.

00:16:55.380 --> 00:16:56.960
I see.

00:17:00.710 --> 00:17:05.670
But anyway, why are you playing boss to those lowlifes?

00:17:05.670 --> 00:17:08.250
They're actually quite candid and likable.

00:17:08.250 --> 00:17:10.710
<i>And why were you picking on them, Momo?</i>

00:17:11.130 --> 00:17:13.880
I was just looking for info on monstrine.

00:17:14.420 --> 00:17:18.500
By the way, I hear you told them to stay away from it.

00:17:18.500 --> 00:17:23.000
Indeed. I saw the Fourth trying to deal it to them.

00:17:23.000 --> 00:17:25.250
That stuff is bad news.

00:17:25.630 --> 00:17:27.130
Aw, I see.

00:17:27.290 --> 00:17:31.830
You aren't famous for going around righting
wrongs for nothing, Princess Justice.

00:17:31.830 --> 00:17:34.880
But you couldn't bear to put up with it either, am I wrong?

00:17:34.880 --> 00:17:37.420
Isn't that why you were so intent on your investigation?

00:17:38.130 --> 00:17:41.250
Shall I share my information with you?

00:17:41.250 --> 00:17:44.710
I already have a lead to where
the drug is being produced.

00:17:45.880 --> 00:17:48.460
I can find that out myself, thank you!

00:17:48.790 --> 00:17:50.830
You don't want to be in my debt?

00:17:51.130 --> 00:17:53.790
Then what if we strike a deal instead?

00:17:53.790 --> 00:17:58.790
I'll give you my information if you'll compete with
me to see who's infiltration gets better results.

00:18:00.500 --> 00:18:01.580
Excuse me?

00:18:02.040 --> 00:18:05.210
I'm planning to investigate a different place.

00:18:05.670 --> 00:18:10.170
The prime suspect behind the distribution
of monstrine is Manon Libelle,

00:18:10.170 --> 00:18:12.670
and this is the invitation to a
ball she's hosting tomorrow evening.

00:18:12.750 --> 00:18:17.750
I don't think you're at all cut out to infiltrate
or investigate anything, Little Princess!

00:18:17.880 --> 00:18:20.830
I'm capable in everything I do.

00:18:21.250 --> 00:18:24.830
I'm confident in my ability to
sniff out a target's vulnerabilities.

00:18:25.630 --> 00:18:28.630
"Sniff out"? That sure sounds impractical!

00:18:28.630 --> 00:18:30.750
You'll compete if you're so confident, then?

00:18:32.580 --> 00:18:38.630
Let us see who manages to get more information.
We'll meet back here at midnight tomorrow.

00:18:40.750 --> 00:18:44.380
So anyway, that crappy little princess was alive.

00:18:44.580 --> 00:18:47.710
How did she wind up as the
boss of some delinquents?

00:18:48.000 --> 00:18:52.210
Well, it's impressive she found out
where the drug is being produced.

00:18:52.210 --> 00:18:54.670
I'm sure she just has too much time on her hands.

00:18:54.670 --> 00:18:58.250
More importantly, about Manon Libelle's evening ball...

00:18:58.250 --> 00:19:00.250
I have information on that already.

00:19:00.250 --> 00:19:04.330
Pastor Sicilia arranged for me to get an invitation.

00:19:04.540 --> 00:19:07.790
I'll have to be careful if the princess is attending as well,

00:19:07.790 --> 00:19:10.330
but I'm just going as a nameless
priestess accompanying the pastor,

00:19:10.330 --> 00:19:11.210
so there shouldn't be any-

00:19:11.210 --> 00:19:14.380
No, you can't! You have to let me make a dress for you!

00:19:14.880 --> 00:19:17.750
You're going to spy on the enemy!

00:19:17.750 --> 00:19:22.040
Why would you dress so obviously
like a priestess in enemy territory?!

00:19:22.250 --> 00:19:25.880
And more importantly,
dressing you up is a mandatory requirement!

00:19:25.880 --> 00:19:29.500
But it's tomorrow evening.
There's no time to be making a dress.

00:19:29.500 --> 00:19:31.540
One night is all I need!

00:19:32.250 --> 00:19:36.500
It's decided, then! Okay, I have to go now!

00:19:36.790 --> 00:19:40.460
Oh well. She doesn't listen once she's in that mode.

00:19:41.500 --> 00:19:44.420
Speaking of not listening, there's that other one...

00:19:44.710 --> 00:19:46.130
I want to go, too!

00:19:46.580 --> 00:19:48.170
I'm going!

00:19:48.170 --> 00:19:50.080
You get to go into that castle, right?

00:19:50.080 --> 00:19:52.460
And only you get to go? It's so not fair!

00:19:52.460 --> 00:19:55.000
It's not a matter of fairness. It's for work!

00:19:55.000 --> 00:19:58.210
What if I get abducted while you're gone?!

00:19:58.210 --> 00:20:02.290
I'll at least say a prayer to our Lord
for the precious life that was lost.

00:20:02.420 --> 00:20:05.210
What?! That's super mean!

00:20:05.290 --> 00:20:08.210
It's not like you have anything you
could wear to a ball, anyway!

00:20:08.210 --> 00:20:10.960
I have my school uniform, okay?

00:20:10.960 --> 00:20:11.630
I wanna go! I wanna go! I wanna go!

00:20:11.630 --> 00:20:15.880
Come on, you know you can't afford to stand out.
I wanna go! I wanna go! I wanna go!<b></b>

00:20:20.330 --> 00:20:24.460
Let's see, I wonder where my darling Menou could be...

00:20:25.830 --> 00:20:28.330
That's Pastor Sicilia there.

00:20:28.330 --> 00:20:30.500
Which must mean somewhere nearby...

00:20:32.420 --> 00:20:37.540
Ooh! There she is! Aww, she's so lovely!

00:20:37.960 --> 00:20:41.580
I just love it when she's all dressed up!

00:20:41.830 --> 00:20:46.380
Thank you so much Pastor Sicilia,
for allowing such an unreasonable request.

00:20:46.540 --> 00:20:48.500
I don't mind.

00:20:48.710 --> 00:20:54.000
It's better if no one can tell you're a priestess,
and whatever you decide to wear-

00:20:54.000 --> 00:20:56.330
No, not about that.

00:20:58.670 --> 00:21:01.290
What?! Why?!

00:21:01.290 --> 00:21:04.290
Why is Boobalicious there?!

00:21:04.290 --> 00:21:09.290
Menou! How do I look?
I'm a pure, just, and strong priestess!

00:21:09.750 --> 00:21:12.040
Um, Pastor Sicilia...

00:21:12.040 --> 00:21:15.960
Thank you for arranging an invitation for Akari as well...

00:21:17.250 --> 00:21:21.960
I must say I'm a little worried,
but she's your responsibility.

00:21:22.380 --> 00:21:23.210
Excuse me.

00:21:25.920 --> 00:21:28.790
Hey! Wait for me, Menou!

00:21:28.880 --> 00:21:34.960
Why does Boobalicious get to see Menou in the
dress I made for her up close when I don't?!

00:21:34.960 --> 00:21:36.960
I can't take this!

00:21:38.170 --> 00:21:39.920
If I want to quell this rage I'm feeling,

00:21:39.920 --> 00:21:43.830
I have to destroy the place they
produce monstrine at the very least!

00:21:47.130 --> 00:21:49.630
Thank you so much for coming, everyone.

00:21:50.000 --> 00:21:52.670
I do hope you'll enjoy the evening.

00:21:52.920 --> 00:21:56.540
I've prepared a plentiful feast for you to enjoy as well.

00:22:01.210 --> 00:22:02.750
Manon Libelle...

00:23:36.000 --> 00:23:40.380
<b>Next Episode</b>

00:23:36.000 --> 00:23:40.380
<b>At the Evening Ball</b>

00:23:36.380 --> 00:23:39.250
Next episode: At the Evening Ball
